WEBVTT

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.830
Maria Watches Over Us

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:16.140
Spreading a blank map wide open
Shiroi chizu ookiku hiroge

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:23.120
Let's go hide the treasure box
Takara-bako kakushi ni ikou

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:31.190
No need for coats or even hats
Kooto nante iranai boushi mo ne

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:38.830
Armed with just mechanical pencil lead
Shaapen no shin dake haite

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.240
Round and round and round,
Kururu kururu ku

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.140
Running through
kakenukeru

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.110
Round and round and round,
Kururu kururu ku

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:54.070
Our footprints mark the X
ashiato wa batsu-jirushi da yo

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:01.090
Passing through the walls of the school
Kousha no kabe tsuki-nuke

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:09.330
We can go anywhere, there will be a path there
Dokonimo ikeru soko ni michi ga aru

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:16.530
The pleats of our skirts won't be disturbed
Sukaato no hida midare-nai

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:23.870
If it's a secret journey
Himitsu no tabi nara

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.510
Don't go.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.720
It's okay, Mom.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.560
Don't go anywhere.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.720
Don't leave Mommy behind.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:44.660
Please...

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.990
Yes, I'm right here.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.730
Where have you gone? My baby...

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.750
Keyhole of the Heart

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.520
Oh, Dad, welcome home.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.830
I didn't know you were still up.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.230
Yes...

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.060
Is something wrong?

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.770
I was staying by Mom's side.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.710
Because she seemed to be having
some trouble falling asleep.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.170
I see.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.940
I'm sorry for getting home so late.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:36.450
Dad...

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.190
I guess it's my fault.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.580
Absolutely not.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.720
So this is how you've always strained
to keep yourself bottled up...

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.260
You're reading too much into this, Dad.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.260
Not once have I ever felt like
I was straining myself.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.710
Our quarrel that day seems to have
come as a shock to your mom,

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:03.440
but if you hadn't poured out
your feelings to us,

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.480
we would probably have remained oblivious...

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.740
...to how your heart was crying out.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.150
At the age of 16, it must have been such...

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.420
...a heavy burden for you to bear alone.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:19.150
That is a burden that we parents
should have been carrying.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.390
That's why,

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.530
even now, I'm in agreement with
your grandfather's decision.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.540
You should pay no mind to who you might be...

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.540
...and freely paint your life upon a blank canvas.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.910
Isn't life about give and take?

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.840
Is it all right for me to just
take all that's given to me?

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.880
I have nothing to give back.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:54.320
Your mom and your grandfather and I
have already received a lot from you.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.400
Drama Club

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.240
Oh, Toko-chan!

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.400
Good day.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.670
My apologies for my recent prolonged absence.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.440
The election... That was too bad.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:17.410
Not at all.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:24.280
Club President, I have come today
for a club resignation form.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.760
What are you saying?!

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.730
As I said...

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.250
Is this related to you losing the election?

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.260
No. I am doing this for personal reasons.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.770
I thought this day might come someday...

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.240
Once I retire from the club to
deal with applying to colleges,

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.770
you might become isolated within the club.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:52.580
You see, I'd like for you to become
the face of the Drama Club.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.790
I don't care in what capacity you do it.
I want you to remain with the club.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:00.520
Our members could learn a lot
from you as an actress.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.470
If you find it hard to get along with
our upperclassmen members,

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.230
I have an idea.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.400
Become my little sister.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.530
Pardon?

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.710
As the little sister of the club president,

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.770
you probably won't face as
much opposition, right?

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.910
The effect won't wear off so easily,
even into the next school year.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.970
But, I...

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.380
Fukuzawa Yumi-san?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.410
I believe I understand.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:29.860
You like Yumi-san, right?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:33.720
I've watched you all this time, after all.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:39.270
If you could find happiness by
becoming Yumi-san's little sister,

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.130
I thought that would be fine.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.870
But every time you get close to Yumi-san,

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.530
you come back wounded.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:49.640
I am sure the problem lies with me.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:50.810
Yes.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.870
If you don't change, you'll never be
able to walk side by side with Yumi-san.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.990
And that's why,

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:02.060
to distance yourself from the Yamayuri
Council and the Rose Mansion,

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.650
you ran in the election that you
were bound to lose, right?

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:09.160
It hurts me to watch you suffering like this.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.370
Just forget about Yumi-san now.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.170
I'll protect you.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.380
I am sorry.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:32.320
I must never choose the club president...

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.590
...in order to cut myself off from Yumi-sama.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:37.690
Toko.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.350
What's this?

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.960
I was lying in wait.

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:46.670
So that I wouldn't stand out.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:50.700
What do you want?

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.670
I wanted to ask you something.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.700
About what happened during Christmas.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.540
Why did you say such a thing to Yumi-chan?

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.010
"Such a thing"?

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.680
I don't understand what your feelings are on this.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.380
I know you like Yumi-chan.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.220
Who did you hear this from?

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:08.450
I can tell just by watching.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.460
You're not very convincing.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:13.690
Then let me ask you this.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.430
Why didn't you go to Canada last summer?

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.630
You heard that Yumi-chan was going
to the Ogasawara's vacation home...

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.370
...and you changed your plans, right?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.300
T-That was...

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.740
At the time,

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.340
I thought you were jealous of Yumi-chan...

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.300
...and you decided to go
so you could come between them.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.810
But that wasn't it.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.880
You were worried about Yumi-chan.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.240
What are you saying?

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:41.510
Because you knew those young
ladies were dangerous.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.890
How would my going there
have changed anything?

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:50.820
Even so, you were too concerned to
go to some distant foreign country.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.070
I get it!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:08:01.130
You were afraid that Yumi-chan would be
bullied in the same way that you were!

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.950
Who in the world was it?!
What did they say?! And when?!

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.650
Was it Kyogoku?! Or Ayanokoji?! Or Saionji?!

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.110
Onii-sama...

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.420
I wasn't able to pick up on it.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.560
Until the moment you ran away from home,

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.190
I believed that you knew nothing!

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.160
Onii-sama?

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:35.310
Onii-sama, I need to pee!

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.070
What?!

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:37.680
Wild Burger
Drive Thru

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.240
You saved me back there.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.980
That could've gotten dicey
if you hadn't stopped me.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.850
You saved me, too.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.410
By getting me to the washroom in time.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:57.150
Onii-sama, it didn't come as
such a shock to me, you know.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:02.130
I had found out long ago.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:05.770
So you needn't be so angry.

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:07.370
Toko...

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.170
You're allowed to find happiness, you know.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.180
What do you mean?

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:16.320
You're running away from the happiness
that's right in front of you.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.990
And that goes for the thing with Yumi-chan, too.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.480
That's over already!

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:33.200
Then are you saying that I should have
accepted the rosary back then?

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.940
Yumi-chan chose you to be her little sister?

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.400
What are you acting so surprised for?

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.870
I didn't know.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.540
At least, not the details of what
happened between you and Yumi-chan.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.050
That's why I baited you into telling me.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.040
Don't tell such an obvious lie!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.550
Why are you always so distrustful?

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:53.450
If I'm to believe in people only to be betrayed,

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.720
it's better not to believe at all!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.850
Wrong.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.690
You say you don't believe,

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:00.890
but in your heart, you want to believe!

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.800
You run, waiting for someone to come after you.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:04.970
That's not...

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.670
If you keep running like that,

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:10.570
soon, there'll be no one coming
after you anymore.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.240
You all lay the blame on me, don't you?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.170
It's probably because we all love you.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.640
You blame me because you love me?

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.050
I don't really understand that.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:28.180
The world's full of things we don't understand.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:35.130
This is what you laid in wait for me to find out?

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.860
Why go to such trouble?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.090
I just wanted to know...

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.400
...what happened between you and Yumi-chan.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.460
Why did you want to know?

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.070
If you think carefully about it, you'll figure it out.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.480
If I think carefully...

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:01.210
Event Set!!
Where are the future Lady Roses' cards?!

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.310
A treasure hunt, huh?

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:23.840
It was exactly a year ago
during last year's treasure hunt...

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:25.850
Oh, look over there!
It was exactly a year ago
during last year's treasure hunt...

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:27.310
It was exactly a year ago
during last year's treasure hunt...

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.850
...that I first saw her.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.090
She was so vivacious...

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.450
...and open and honest.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.360
This was the person Sachiko
Onee-sama had chosen.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:43.830
I found her frightening.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.800
I didn't know why.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:49.030
She just... scared me in an indefinable way.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.100
And yet, before I knew it, I...

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.230
Toko-chan!

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:00.110
It's so stupid!

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.410
So stupid! So stupid! So stupid! So stupid!

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.420
Well, then, good-bye, ladies.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:10.390
See you later!

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:11.550
Good-bye!

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.620
Toko.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.900
You seem busy.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.420
Are you headed for the Rose Mansion?

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:20.890
Nope. I have the day off today.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.470
I'm in a hurry because there's going to
be a TV special on Buddhist statues.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:26.430
I see.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.200
Well, good-bye.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:32.970
Noriko-san!

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.040
What is it?

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.550
What?

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:37.240
Um...

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:41.480
It must be tough.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.120
You'll be one of the people hiding
the treasure this year, right?

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:48.390
No, the three second-years are
going to be hiding the treasure.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.130
It's on here, if I recall...

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:51.930
Do you have one of these?

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.230
No...

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:55.570
Then you can have it.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:56.400
What?

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:00.270
I've already read it and I can always
look at it at the Rose Mansion.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:02.730
See you.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:26.020
The three second-years are
going to be hiding the treasure.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:35.140
Oh?

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:36.970
Good day.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:40.510
G-Good day.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.610
Were you on your way home?

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:44.650
Yes...

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.050
Then, we can go together to the station.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.450
Was there something you
wished to see me about?

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:54.720
I don't know...

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.630
It's like how you impulsively
call out to stop your friend,

00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:01.120
but afterwards, you have to
think about why you did that.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.540
Does that make no sense?

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:04.630
Not at all...

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:06.630
Toko-chan.

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:09.530
I'm sorry for being unreasonable.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.440
It was thoughtless of me.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:16.540
I offered you my rosary
before I had thought it through.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.990
I didn't give proper consideration
to your feelings or anything...

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:23.890
...and I just forged ahead,
acting on my emotions alone.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:26.590
I think it's not surprising that
you found it appalling.

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.660
All of that is my apology.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:31.500
And this is where my proposal comes in, but...

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:34.830
Can't we possibly go back to the
relationship we had before Christmas?

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:39.440
I do not understand what is
in your heart, Yumi-sama!

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:43.370
Why are you so generous towards an
underclassman who rejected you?!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.210
What?

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:45.650
And to begin with,

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:48.850
why did you think to make someone
like me your little sister anyway?!

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:51.580
Please don't put yourself down
and say "someone like me."

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:52.980
Someone like me...

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.950
"Someone like me" is good enough!

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:59.330
It was a momentary lapse
of judgment on your part.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.530
That was how I interpreted it.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:03.360
And I was satisfied with that.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.490
So why do you bother yourself about me?!

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:08.300
Don't you know?

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:21.110
You know, since you turned me down,
I've been thinking all this time.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:25.050
I wondered what was going
to happen to you and me.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:29.580
But it came to me that I should
think about what I want to happen.

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:32.560
That's when I figured it out.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:38.030
That all I want is for you to be you.

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:42.660
For me to be me?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.770
That's right.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.710
So, no matter what you do,

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.840
it won't change how I feel.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:53.280
Even the reason you ran for student council...

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.110
If you don't want me to ask, I won't pry.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:01.580
The same goes for things like
why you ran away from home.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.430
What kind of people your parents are...

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.890
What your relationship is with them now...

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.330
What kind of childhood you had...

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:15.770
Because those things are on a completely
different plane of existence...

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:18.140
...from my feelings for you.

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:24.510
I see.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:26.510
So that's it.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.170
What?

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:31.750
What you did then ultimately stemmed
from your pity for me, didn't it?!

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:36.090
You only wanted to bestow
Christmas Eve charity upon me!

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:40.660
It must have felt so good when
you offered me that rosary!

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:46.090
As long as I'm myself? My parents don't matter?!

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:48.000
I knew something was strange!

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.070
There was no reason you would
want me for your little sister!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.010
But now, the mystery is finally solved!

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.530
What are you saying?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:58.640
If you were doing it without
realizing it, that's even worse!

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:00.180
I think there's some misunderstanding...

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:01.510
Please stay where you are!

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.580
Don't come any closer!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:04.910
Toko-chan...

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.950
I don't want to hear your excuses!

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:15.050
All right.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:18.820
It doesn't look like you're willing
to listen, no matter what I say.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:25.040
Toko-chan.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:28.580
Stay there and count to one-hundred.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:31.370
Don't you move until you've finished counting.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.940
One. Two. Three. Four.

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:43.950
Five. Six. Seven. Eight.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:48.590
Nine. Ten. Eleven. Twelve.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:53.730
Thirteen. Fourteen. Fifteen. Sixteen.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:59.100
Forty-seven. Forty-eight. Forty-nine. Fifty.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:04.780
Ninety-five. Ninety-six. Ninety-seven. Ninety-eight.

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:07.310
Ninety-nine. One-hundred.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.720
My! Really?

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.050
Pardon me!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.320
Is something the matter?

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:23.560
Did you tell Yumi-sama?

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:24.730
What is this about?

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:26.020
That is...

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:28.800
Speak plainly.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:33.060
It seems you have come to me
to air some grievance,

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:36.170
but I will not be able to understand
unless you speak plainly.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:39.380
About matters concerning my birth.

00:18:39.650 --> 00:18:40.980
About your birth?

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:43.480
You must know what I mean!

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:46.680
So? When did you tell Yumi-sama?!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.320
As I said, tell her what?

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.960
Please do not play dumb!

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:53.690
I'm talking about how I'm
not the Matsudairas' child!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.590
Toko-chan...

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:02.860
You were not born to Mr. and Mrs. Matsudaira?

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:05.830
Surely not...

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.540
I'm sorry, but this is news to me.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.470
You're lying...

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.340
It is the truth.

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:13.000
It cannot be...

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:16.410
Then, who could have told Yumi-sama?

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.410
Suguru Onii-sama?

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:22.950
No, he showed no signs of that.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:28.490
Honestly! What a low opinion you must have!

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:31.700
I am so very sorry.

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:34.270
Not me. I meant of Yumi.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:39.030
I'm sure Yumi knows nothing
of your family background.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.210
Even if she did find out by accident,

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:46.200
she's not the sort of girl to think
differently of you based on that.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.720
As her big sister, I know that better than anyone.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:01.930
And yet, Yumi has devoted
so much thought to you,

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:03.620
I'm beginning to feel sorry for her.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.990
Then, it was all...

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:11.500
...my misunderstanding?

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:26.490
Yumi-sama...

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:31.480
I don't know what I should do anymore.

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:34.060
Stay there and count to one-hundred.

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:39.860
One. Two. Three.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:44.370
Four. Five. Six.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:45.640
Seven. Eight. Nine.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.540
I'm all alone now.
Seven. Eight. Nine.

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:49.200
Seven. Eight. Nine.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.180
All the ties I had with everyone...

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.850
All the ties I had with everyone...
Ten. Eleven. Twelve. Thirteen.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:55.420
One by one, I severed them myself...
Ten. Eleven. Twelve. Thirteen.

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:55.740
Ten. Eleven. Twelve. Thirteen.

00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:59.180
Thirty-one. Thirty-two.

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:00.850
Thirty-three. Thirty-four.

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:03.720
But I'm so terribly lonely...
Thirty-three. Thirty-four.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:03.920
But I'm so terribly lonely...

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:05.390
Thirty-five. Thirty-six.

00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:08.190
I don't care who it is, I want someone by my side.
Thirty-five. Thirty-six.

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:12.800
Soon, there'll be no one
coming after you anymore.

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:15.940
Fifty-six. Fifty-seven.

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:16.800
I'm scared to count.
Fifty-six. Fifty-seven.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:17.740
I'm scared to count.

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:20.210
Fifty-eight. Fifty-nine. Sixty.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:23.380
To open my eyes and find myself all alone...
Fifty-eight. Fifty-nine. Sixty.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:24.540
To open my eyes and find myself all alone...

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:27.680
Seventy-five. Seventy-six.

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:31.580
Seventy-seven. Seventy-eight.

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:37.850
Seventy-nine. Eighty. Eighty-one.

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:43.090
Oh, sorry.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:45.960
I did think that maybe
I shouldn't disturb you, but...

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:48.970
Why? I thought you went home...

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:51.970
After I said good-bye to you,
something about it bothered me.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:54.910
But what about the special?

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:57.700
What you want to talk to me about
is more important than that.

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:04.840
Noriko!

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:06.450
Noriko!

00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:07.950
What?

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:09.350
Noriko...

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:11.490
What in the world is wrong?

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.560
Maria-sama, thank you so much!

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:19.520
For bringing Noriko back to me.

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:25.200
Noriko...

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:29.300
Noriko...

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:47.790
A winterscape where even...
Machi no irodori sae doko

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:52.560
...the town's colors seem forlorn somehow
to naku samishige na fuyu no keshiki

00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:56.570
I think of you, turning your back on me...
Senaka mise kaketeitta

00:22:56.570 --> 00:23:00.300
...and running off
anata o omou

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:05.280
There's a clear square pane...
Futari no aida ni wa

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:09.280
...between the two of us
toumei na shikakkei

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:12.050
It's misted over right now...
Ima wa kasunderu

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:18.650
...with the crystals of sighs
tame-iki no kesshou de

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:23.300
Window glass, window glass
Mado garasu mado garasu

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:29.270
It's clouded and I can't see you
Kumottete anata ga mienai no

00:23:29.270 --> 00:23:35.070
Even though I know that you're there
Soko ni iru koto wa wakatteiru no ni

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:39.210
Are you smiling? Are you crying?
Waratteru naiteru no

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:45.220
I don't even care if you're frowning, let me see you
Shikamettsura demo ii kara misete

00:23:45.220 --> 00:23:53.680
Wipe the glass from your side, too
Sochira no hou kara mo garasu o fuite

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:07.010
Preview

00:24:07.010 --> 00:24:08.480
Preview
Today is Valentine's Day.

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:10.140
Preview
Amazingly, even Mami-san
from the school paper...

00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:12.680
Preview
...received chocolates from
Hidemi, her little sister.

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:14.380
Preview
What? Chocolates for me?!

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:16.420
Preview
Mami-san, the first thing you
should say is "thank you."

00:24:16.420 --> 00:24:17.850
Preview
You didn't have to say that's the "first thing."

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.920
Preview
And also, "I'm so happy."

00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:21.590
Preview
I-I'm so happy!

00:24:21.590 --> 00:24:23.960
Preview
But I am the ogre of the Lillian Ledger!

00:24:23.960 --> 00:24:26.630
Preview
I can't be all merry just
because it's Valentine's Day!

00:24:26.630 --> 00:24:27.290
Preview
I can't be all merry just
because it's Valentine's Day!
Crisscross

00:24:27.290 --> 00:24:29.030
Preview
Next time, "Crisscross."
Crisscross

00:24:29.030 --> 00:24:31.400
Preview
I wonder what will happen
in this year's treasure hunt.
Crisscross

00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:34.170
Preview
Who will be the ones to find our cards?
Crisscross

00:24:34.170 --> 00:24:35.900
Preview
Crisscross
